<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U shares fall after CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U shares fall after CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs company Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn shares fell on Monday after the company said its chief executive John Zabriskie had resigned.</p>
<p>At 1255 GMT the share was10 crowns lower at 274 crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;I think people are a little nervous, waiting to find out what this means,&quot; said one London-based drugs sector analyst.</p>
<p>&quot;There were two profit warnings last year so it could be related to that or it could mean there is more bad news to come. The stock has been marked down on the latter.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
